decisions:
  - id: neverland-open-standard
    decision: Neverland is an open registry for any AI tool — not Paradigm-specific. skill.yaml is a public open standard.
    rationale: 'User confirmed: true goal is agents + skills for anyone in the world / for organizations. Paradigm is reference implementation.'
  - id: no-auto-bundle-v1
    decision: Bundle auto-install cut from v1. Skills installed separately via CLI after agent install.
    rationale: Dependency graph resolution, partial failure handling, and conflict state management are too risky to ship in 18 days. User experience cost (4 extra commands) is acceptable. v1.1 target.
  - id: signing-optional-v1
    decision: Ed25519 signature field present in skill.yaml format but enforcement optional at v1. Key management UX must be fully specced before enforcement.
    rationale: Contradicted existing architectural decision to defer key management UX. Field present now avoids breaking change when enforcement ships.
  - id: cf-workers-r2-stack
    decision: Infrastructure stack is Cloudflare Workers + R2 + KV. Must be confirmed Day 1.
    rationale: 18-day schedule is only valid on this stack. Traditional server stack (Express + PostgreSQL + S3) invalidates the sequencing.
  - id: semver-behavioral-definitions
    decision: Major version = fundamentally different behavioral contract. Minor = additive. Patch = prose improvement. Must be documented before conflict detection is implemented.
    rationale: Semver compatibility semantics for prompt bodies are undefined without this. Conflict detection logic is semantically empty without the definition.
